{"id": "EUVD-2026-48930", "enisaUuid": "214bd02f-83fe-3ab7-8716-801753055119", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix query_info() replay double-free\n\nA response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its\nresponse buffer. If SMB2_query_info_init() fails before the next send,\ncleanup retains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.\n\nReset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:26", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/100fb7c455fa86d248b8bd7bb9de757c192870b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c81dda84799f76b42aec598564316e2964440db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1add4acb656f5a82806a1ab0e63fed3d8b1bfca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89234773e8348918111aa15f6922b58cf3843364", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a88561d66eb855813cf004a0abe648bbb17de5e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5v7v-hhr9-43wj", "CVE-2026-64386"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c61addd-a7b1-3ca9-a899-57bbc8fc6f1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <f1add4acb656f5a82806a1ab0e63fed3d8b1bfca"}, {"id": "284d54ce-24ff-3906-b1be-51516bc5d2e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "433042a91f9373241307725b52de573933ffedbf <100fb7c455fa86d248b8bd7bb9de757c192870b4"}, {"id": "326580d6-d3e8-3aae-abc6-657d278c1665", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "630f3977-da5b-30ff-ae11-40cb8def5a55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "73d3247e-945f-31d9-b62a-0fc74b2684bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendo